#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""bd-footguns -- an EXECUTABLE footgun registry.

The problem this fixes: hard-won footguns live as PROSE (STATE.active_footguns, KB
docs). Prose can be forgotten, mis-remembered, or phrased as a mechanism that drifts
from the real gate -- exactly what shipped the v3.66.699 env-tranche regression.
A footgun that is a RUNNABLE DETECTOR cannot be forgotten: it runs pre-cut, every
cut, and it DELEGATES to the authoritative check (a tool or an in-sync test) so it
cannot drift.

Each footgun binds: a stable id, an observable RULE (invariant, not mechanism), a
DETECTOR (delegate to the real gate), the tests it PROTECTS, PROVENANCE (which cut
introduced it / which cut it bit), the FIX, and STATUS.

  bd-footguns --check [--tree DIR]     run every active detector; exit 3 on a
                                       BLOCKING violation (wire before bd-cut).
                                       --tree defaults to the checkout this tool
                                       lives in. Exit 2 = CANNOT-EVALUATE: not one
                                       detector reached a verdict, so "no footgun
                                       violated" would be a report over nothing.
  bd-footguns --list [--json]          the registry (human/machine).
  bd-footguns --explain ID             one footgun in full.
  bd-footguns --selftest               neg + pos controls.

External FOOTGUNS.json (tree root or alongside this tool) is merged over the
embedded seed, so the registry grows with the project without editing the tool.
"""
import argparse, ctypes, errno, json, os, platform, re, shutil, stat
import subprocess, sys, tempfile

# v3.66.855 desandbox. AFTER the import line on purpose (sys must already be bound).
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
import bdtools_sec as sec  # noqa: E402

